From: Project Arctic
Subject: uxtheme: a theme change never waits for a window.

WM_THEMECHANGED went to every window of every program with SendMessageW:
one window that did not answer held the thread that changed the visual
style for good. In explorer that was the thread of Personalization, and
every later change waited behind it, so the style of Windows 11 could not
be chosen again after Windows 10's (2026-11-21). The message is sent with
SendNotifyMessageW: the windows of the calling thread still get it at once,
the others when their thread reads its messages. The sender keeps nothing
the receivers need: each of them loads the active theme itself.
---
diff --git a/dll/win32/uxtheme/system.c b/dll/win32/uxtheme/system.c
--- a/dll/win32/uxtheme/system.c
+++ b/dll/win32/uxtheme/system.c
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@

 static BOOL CALLBACK UXTHEME_send_theme_changed (HWND hWnd, LPARAM enable)
 {
-    SendMessageW(hWnd, WM_THEMECHANGED, enable, 0);
+    SendNotifyMessageW(hWnd, WM_THEMECHANGED, enable, 0);
     return TRUE;
 }

